# What this file is for
#
# vercel.json sets "outputDirectory": "." — the whole repo root is the site.
# That means every committed file here becomes a public URL on mintraiq.com.
# There is no build step that selects what ships; if it is in the repo, it is
# on the internet.
#
# Everything listed below is internal working material that would otherwise be
# published. Do not remove a line without checking what it exposes.
#
# marketing/ — content planning and compliance working files:
#   pillars.md  states where our Fair Trading Act / FMCA Part 6 line sits, and
#               records that the automated copy test cannot catch a novel false
#               claim in fresh wording.
#   calendar.md is the twelve-week content plan.
#   reels/*/claims.md carry internal code references and, in at least one case,
#               a written record of a past user-facing defect.
# None of it is secret. All of it is material we would never choose to publish
# under our own domain, permanently and indexably.
#
# Post images are uploaded to Meta directly and do not need to be served from
# here, so the whole directory is excluded rather than picked over.
#
# Added 2026-09-21 alongside the week-1 social package merge (PRIORITIES G #63).

marketing/

#
# legacy/ — 69 committed files: a superseded Flask-era application, including
#   legacy/pages/{account-profile,budget-planner,cpi-guru,financial-score,
#   forecast,goals}.html and legacy/static-flask/account.js, which POSTs to
#   /api/create-checkout-session. Every one of them was a live public URL on
#   mintraiq.com. legacy/templates/*.html are Jinja templates that render as
#   broken markup but stay readable, exposing internal API shapes.
#   Excluded 2026-09-22 alongside deleting that route (PRIORITIES G #65): with
#   the route gone those pages' upgrade buttons would 404 in public.

legacy/

# --- Verified live on 27 Sep 2026, before this change ---------------------
#
# Each of these returned content, not a 404, at https://mintraiq.com/<path>.
# Checked with a real browser: curl is rate-limited by the edge and returns 429,
# which reads like "blocked" and is not.
#
#   /.cursor/security.md            our internal security and compliance standards
#   /.github/workflows/cd.yml       the deploy workflow — env var and secret NAMES,
#                                   Cloud Run service names, the whole pipeline
#   /docs/openapi.json              the full dashboard API spec, every route
#   /scripts/build-runtime-env.mjs  the build script and its endpoint defaults
#
# Vercel has a small denylist of its own: /.env.vars and /package.json already
# 404. Do not infer from that that dotfiles are safe — dot-DIRECTORIES are
# served, which is exactly how .cursor/ and .github/ were public.

.cursor/
.claude/
.github/
.agents/
.superpowers/
.cursorrules
..cursorignore

docs/
e2e/
test-results/

README.md
config.example.json
env.public.example
*.py

# scripts/ is NOT excluded wholesale, and package.json is not excluded at all:
# vercel.json sets "buildCommand": "npm run build", which runs
# scripts/build-runtime-env.mjs to generate config/runtime-env.js. Ignoring
# either breaks the build, not just the page. (package.json already 404s on its
# own — Vercel denylists it — so leaving it is not an exposure.)
#
# Everything else in scripts/ is test-only and was being served.
scripts/*.test.mjs
scripts/social-copy-rules.mjs
scripts/serve.sh

# Deliberately NOT excluded, though they look internal: mock-dashboard.html,
# designs.html, intro-neon-a/b/c.html, layout.html and home.html are each linked
# from a shipped page, so ignoring them would break live links rather than hide
# anything. intro.html points at the dashboard demo on purpose. Whether those
# pages should be public at all is a content decision, not a config one — raise
# it separately rather than fixing it here.
